WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
A balanced equation says a reaction
should make 10 grams of product.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.910
A chemist carries it out carefully,
and collects only 7 grams.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.770
Three grams short.

4
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.330
So why is the yield lower
than the equation promised?

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:19.790
If the equation promises 10 grams of product,
why do chemists often collect only 7?

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.610
In this mission, you'll
calculate percentage yield,

7
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.930
and find out what pulls
it below 100 percent.

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.470
You'll solve a combined problem, from
limiting reactant to final yield,

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.170
and work backwards from a yield
to the reactants you need.

10
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: explain why the yield falls
short of what the equation promises.
